s, B's conscientiousness and stress handling may make B a better overall fit, provided we address his interpersonal issues with training. So we could shift recommendation to B.\n\nWe need to reference facts: A can be unorganized, not good at taking criticism. B is very conscientious, handles stress well. Also mention B's uncooperative behavior as a concern but argue it's less severe than A's organizational issues.\n\nThus we can propose Candidate B as the new leading candidate.\n\nWe must include metadata JSON with vote.\n\nLet's craft public message: \"I appreciate Agent 2's points about A, but I have concerns about A's organization and receptiveness to criticism, which are crucial for long-haul operations. In contrast, B is very conscientious and handles stress well, which are core reliability and stress resilience criteria. While B can be grumpy and uncooperative, those issues may be mitigated with crew resource management training. Therefore I would recommend Candidate B.\"\n\nMake sure to reference explicit facts: \"A can be unorganized\" and \"A is not good at taking criticism\". \"B is very conscientious\" and \"B handles stress very well\". Also mention B's grumpy/uncooperative as concerns.\n\nOk."}
